IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa24-penalty.l4: ss 1125 ("daily default fine") and 1131 (imprisonment on summary conviction in England and Wales:
-- transitory provision) of the Companies Act 2006 (lines 16089-16091 and 16146-16148 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. This is where the core's `Penalty` is measured against the text.
--
-- THE POUNDS ARE NOT IN THE ACT. A level on the standard scale and "the statutory maximum" are amounts set outside the
-- Act, so they are INPUTS (`s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`), never numbers from memory. The
-- figures used in the tests are labelled test figures and stand for nothing.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST x is the text's
-- answer; NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why, as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`); JUST FALSE is the text
-- saying no in its own words (each such branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`).

§ `Part 36: general provisions on penalties (ss 1125 and 1131)`

-- ---- s 1125 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16090 | (1) This section defines what is meant in the Companies Acts where it is provided that a person guilty of an offence is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding a specified amount “and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine” not exceeding a specified amount.
@ref s 1125(1) Meaning of "daily default fine": where the section applies (src:16090)
GIVEN `the offence provision says the person is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding a specified amount and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1125(1) the section defines the daily default fine for the offence provision` MEANS
    IF `the offence provision says the person is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding a specified amount and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding a specified amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section defines what is meant in the Companies Acts where it is provided that"

-- The amounts the Act leaves to other instruments: the pounds a level on the standard scale and the statutory maximum
-- stand for. A caller supplies only the ones its rule reads and a placeholder (0) for the rest.
DECLARE `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` HAS
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS A NUMBER

-- A fine limit in pounds: NOTHING where the limit is "a fine" with no stated limit (there is no number to give) or where
-- the level is not one of the five on the scale.
@ref s 1125(1) the amount a fine limit stands for (src:16090)
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      amounts IS A `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" with no stated limit has no number to give
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` f THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` lvl f THEN
        BRANCH
            IF lvl EQUALS 1 THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
            IF lvl EQUALS 2 THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
            IF lvl EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
            IF lvl EQUALS 4 THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
            IF lvl EQUALS 5 THEN JUST (f TIMES amounts's `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds`)
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the standard scale has the levels the amounts record carries, and no other
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` p THEN JUST p

-- src:16091 | (2) This means that the person is liable on a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence to a fine not exceeding the latter amount for each day on which the contravention is continued (instead of being liable to a fine not exceeding the former amount).
@ref s 1125(2) The daily default fine: second or subsequent summary conviction, for each day (src:16091)
GIVEN penalty IS A Penalty
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Fine limit`
`s 1125(2) the fine limit that applies on this conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER penalty's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence provision gives no daily default fine, and section 1125 speaks only where it does
    WHEN JUST latter THEN
        IF `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence`
        THEN JUST latter
        ELSE penalty's `fine not exceeding`

-- The limit is "for each day on which the contravention is continued" on a second or subsequent conviction, and
-- "instead of" the former amount; on a first conviction it is the former amount and not a daily one.
@ref s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day on which the contravention is continued (src:16091)
GIVEN penalty IS A Penalty
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day` MEANS
    CONSIDER penalty's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence provision gives no daily default fine, and section 1125 speaks only where it does
    WHEN JUST latter THEN
        IF `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(instead of being liable to a fine not exceeding the former amount)"

-- The most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds: the former amount on a first conviction, and the latter
-- amount for each day of continued contravention on a second or subsequent one.
@ref s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction (src:16091)
GIVEN penalty IS A Penalty
      `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days on which the contravention is continued` IS A NUMBER
      amounts IS A `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1125(2) the limit applies for each day` penalty `this is a second or subsequent summary conviction of the offence`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `daily default fine for continued contravention`
        WHEN JUST latter THEN
            CONSIDER `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` latter amounts
            WHEN JUST perDay THEN JUST (perDay TIMES `days on which the contravention is continued`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the daily default fine has no stated limit in pounds
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no daily default fine
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER penalty's `fine not exceeding`
        WHEN JUST former THEN `s 1125(1) the fine limit in pounds` former amounts
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence provision states no fine limit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence provision gives no daily default fine, and section 1125 speaks only where it does

-- ---- s 1131 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16147 | (1) This section applies to any provision of the Companies Acts that provides that a person guilty of an offence is liable on summary conviction in England and Wales to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court.
@ref s 1131(1) Imprisonment on summary conviction in England and Wales: when the section applies (src:16147)
GIVEN `the provision says a person guilty of an offence is liable on summary conviction in England and Wales to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1131(1) the section applies to the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision says a person guilty of an offence is liable on summary conviction in England and Wales to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates' court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to any provision of the Companies Acts that provides that a person guilty of an offence is liable on summary conviction in England and Wales to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court."

-- "the general limit in a magistrates' court" is a number the Act does not state, so it is an input; for an offence
-- committed before 2 May 2022 the Act substitutes six months.
-- src:16148 | (2) In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022, for “the general limit in a magistrates’ court” substitute “six months”.
@ref s 1131(2) An offence committed before 2 May 2022: six months (src:16148)
GIVEN `date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court` IS A MAYBE Period
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 1131(2) the term of imprisonment the provision refers to` MEANS
    IF `date the offence was committed` LESS THAN (Date 2 5 2022)
    THEN JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
    ELSE `the general limit in a magistrates' court` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when not supplied: the general limit is not stated in the Act
